:["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,1],"Message":"","SHA":"4fcfb02c92e8618767c1d9c963394bceebde2e98"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-24T01:06:09Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,1],"Message":"","SHA":"19ce3e7944f7060d1c0a048a614daba75366a6bc"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-23T18:55:38Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,1],"Message":"docs(readme): Add Air component to architecture documentation\n\nThis commit updates the project's README to include the newly introduced Air component, a background daemon written in Rust that handles resource-intensive operations. The documentation now reflects the complete architecture by:\n\n- Adding Air to the main architecture table with its role description and primary technologies\n- Including Air in the elements table with its description and GitHub repository link\n- Updating Mountain's responsibilities to reflect its management of both Cocoon and Air processes\n\nThese changes ensure the documentation accurately represents the current system architecture and provides proper context for developers exploring the codebase.","SHA":"5bff52b7a9154c6b43a3d7eef5c614fc54b24b98"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-23T18:23:40Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,2],"Message":"save\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>","SHA":"90e15de900980cf738b7b9ac5c154564aaeefdb5"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-23T09:54:00Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,1],"Message":"save\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>","SHA":"d2442f994e9f00a33cbdf7c8356dca1b5f3b58a1"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-23T01:09:26Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,1],"Message":"","SHA":"9c47b8f9fe77bd55ebb816bb840530f1485e9547"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-22T18:21:00Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,1],"Message":"","SHA":"07771ee3a05cf7cf435501f81fa4b6a27be4be55"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-22T13:15:25Z","File":["⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,5],"Message":"save\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>","SHA":"aa59ec270e3998082baa84322993efed91cc6921"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-21T22:09:52Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",72,2],"Message":"","SHA":"2ed6b0219d6d399cd593b72bed344d4fb1bde593"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-21T21:55:28Z","File":["⣿⣿⣿⣿⣿",71,300],"Message":"save","SHA":"96a522675c24cc32524a4cb39021dbe9302389db"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-21T21:22:52Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",1920,1],"Message":"","SHA":"8ff444483c829b21a043aa352df5ecf8748d5f5d"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-21T21:14:32Z","File":["⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",1920,300],"Message":"","SHA":"229aafc154ae8a9c81b039755ee61e23a87c6f82"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-20T14:21:09Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,4],"Message":"chore(config): Update code formatting and project configuration\n\nUpdated and refined project-wide formatting and configuration files to improve developer experience and ensure consistency across different file types.\n\n**Key changes made:**\n- **Updated Prettier configuration** (`prettier.config.js`): Completely restructured with detailed comments and organized sections. Added explicit parser overrides for various file types (JavaScript, TypeScript, Astro, Svelte, Lua, TOML, Markdown, and JSON). Separated JSON handling into strict mode for `package.json` (using `json-stringify`) and loose mode for other JSON files (using `json` parser that allows comments). Clarified plugin ordering with TailwindCSS as the last plugin. Added comprehensive import ordering rules.\n- **Updated EditorConfig** (`.editorconfig`): Added a commented section for Rust files (`.rs`) that explicitly unsets certain formatting rules, preventing conflicts with `rustfmt` while maintaining basic file structure preferences.\n- **Updated README** (`README.md`): Minor grammatical adjustment in the technical vision section, replacing em-dashes with plain text for cleaner rendering.\n- **Updated VSCode settings** (`.vscode/settings.json`): The file was significantly modified (576 → 1678 bytes), though the specific content changes are not detailed in the diff. This likely includes workspace-specific editor preferences.\n\nThese changes ensure consistent code formatting across the codebase while accommodating the specific needs of different file types and development workflows. The updated Prettier configuration provides clear documentation for all formatting rules, making it easier for team members to understand and maintain the code style.","SHA":"5432e9793ca69b0cc62ebd0cf3603aab9d5f6ea2"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-20T14:18:30Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,2],"Message":"chore(build): Update Cargo configuration and add Tauri plugins\n\nEnhanced the Rust build configuration for improved development experience and added new Tauri plugin capabilities to the workspace.\n\nIn `.cargo/config.toml`:\n- Added `git-fetch-with-cli = true` under `[net]` for more reliable network operations during dependency fetching.\n- Defined a comprehensive `[profile.dev]` section with incremental compilation enabled (`incremental = true`), debuginfo stripping configured (`strip = \"debuginfo\"`), panic set to abort for cleaner crashes, and optimization level 3 applied to all dependencies via `[profile.dev.package.\"*\"]` for faster development builds.\n- Added target-specific `rustflags` for both Apple architectures (`aarch64-apple-darwin` and `x86_64-apple-darwin`) with `-Zshare-generics=y` flag to potentially reduce binary size through generic sharing.\n\nIn `Cargo.toml`:\n- Added two new Tauri workspace dependencies: `tauri-plugin-localhost` (v2.3.2) for localhost server capabilities and `tauri-plugin-log` (v2.8.0) for enhanced logging functionality.\n- Removed the outdated comment `# Tauri (Mountain)` that was no longer relevant.\n- Updated the `rust-version` field from 1.89.0 to 1.95.0 to align with the latest Rust toolchain requirements and ensure compatibility with newer language features.","SHA":"6070b459d2b1264583e6f591ea4e5e6b4de8c06d"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-19T11:58:32Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,2],"Message":"chore(deps): Update dependencies and adjust rustfmt configuration\n\n- Added the `dynamic-acl` feature to the `tauri` dependency.\n- Updated `thiserror` from version `2.0.17` to `2.0.18`.\n- Corrected formatting in `tonic-prost` dependency entry by removing extra whitespace.\n- Modified `rustfmt.toml` to disable `remove_nested_parens`, `reorder_impl_items`, `reorder_imports`, and `reorder_modules` to align with updated code style preferences.","SHA":"1f13d771a72decba1463077e08d5b406af9c3af4"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T09:16:19Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,3],"Message":"save\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>","SHA":"143b58eee5fd74ee9f727d0bdf4bd7e671495e04"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T08:02:02Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,1],"Message":"","SHA":"ae772a5cfa7fcc7f1c6a1e59b9ff8ad998f483b6"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T08:01:19Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,2],"Message":"","SHA":"bb80104e4024d975f1e1828f6e26d662a7b64af0"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T07:37:17Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,3],"Message":"save\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>","SHA":"f1726ea85c55d2c462b619bce4365f9769f2873e"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T07:22:29Z","File":["⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,3],"Message":"","SHA":"2f0ae175362e9df3cd16456f1f5266f71c8c88e9"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T06:32:34Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,1],"Message":"chore(deps): Update Rust dependencies in Cargo.toml\n\nThis commit updates several Rust crate dependencies in the project's Cargo.toml file. The changes include both version updates and new dependency additions aimed at improving functionality and maintaining compatibility with the latest versions.\n\nKey updates:\n- Updated `prost` from pinned version `0.13.5` to `0.14.3`, removing the strict version pin and allowing for more flexible version resolution.\n- Added `tonic-prost-build` and `tonic-prost` dependencies (both version `0.14.2`) to support Protocol Buffers integration with Tonic gRPC framework.\n- Reorganized dependency ordering: moved `fs_extra` (version `1.3.0`) to an earlier position in the list and placed `tonic-prost` at the end.\n- Downgraded `toml` from `0.9.11` to `0.9.8` and `toml_edit` from `0.24.0` to `0.23.9`, possibly to address compatibility issues or revert to more stable versions.\n\nThese dependency changes align with ongoing maintenance efforts to keep the Rust backend dependencies current and ensure proper integration between Tonic gRPC services and Protocol Buffers serialization.","SHA":"db138b648b63749b031ddf1857d0e9f3cb8d9c5c"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T03:13:33Z","File":["⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",70,1],"Message":"Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Land into Current","SHA":"866954ca975d8fc708a692f78a222926f20a09e4"},{"Author":"Nikola Hristov","Date":"2026-01-18T03:13:26Z","File":["⣿⡿⠀⠀⠀",70,26],"Message":"chore(deps): Update dependencies and GitHub Actions workflows\n\nThis commit updates various dependencies across the project, including Rust crates, Node.js packages, and GitHub Actions versions. Key updates include:\n\n- Updated Tauri dependencies (tauri, tauri-plugin-dialog, tauri-plugin-fs) to newer versions.\n- Bumped numerous Rust crate versions in Cargo.toml.\n- Updated several devDependencies in package.json, such as @biomejs/biome, prettier, tailwindcss, and turbo.\n- Upgraded GitHub Actions in workflow files: actions/checkout, actions/setup-node, pnpm/action-setup, actions/upload-artifact, and actions/cache.\n- Removed --provenance flag from npm publish command in NPM.yml workflow.\n- Changed link-workspace-packages setting in .npmrc from true to deep.\n- Removed extends field from turbo.json.\n- Deleted multiple IntelliJ IDEA configuration files (.idea/*) that were previously tracked.\n- Updated Element and Dependency submodules to their latest commits.\n\nThese changes aim to keep the project up-to-date with the latest tooling and dependency improvements, potentially bringing performance enhancements, bug fixes, and new features. Removing the IntelliJ configuration files reduces repository clutter, assuming these are user-specific settings.","SHA":"3c4cf0089f696e47e25521e0589bf68dd8f3a2a6"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-16T00:11:30Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"16d42390bb70e147fbaff39d3a41844c05bf6d88"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-15T00:11:29Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"892e4f56331a49764760dbce44bf5d20f503c221"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-14T00:11:31Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"8e1fcdcc30d3a336b6da7c38cb148e7c4d59deaa"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-13T00:09:00Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"887254c108bb327a7d21ad23387fdac48ab35db9"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-12T00:11:45Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"289ec02ee10f6f6234bda78b83dba63244211c67"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-11T00:12:17Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"4d00257ac2d065c1e53c7122b9dd382e71953d21"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-10T00:10:51Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"ea64d38f693ef5b81f3a5b9dfe2d874c5fde367c"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-09T01:08:33Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"2a15fbdba8e8656de5ac0c3fe661d139a1a37160"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-08T01:07:57Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"3725ce78afd361f6c909b51cdfe6e1b3feb8bc0e"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-07T01:08:03Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"882873a03fd13a98eab21ae20489a024003b0b00"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-06T01:07:45Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"12ee5644596ee0ce4634bc5c05a2db2ff035a8fa"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-05T01:13:45Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"d17e477ca97180d6df0fbed517ebe1e4d11378b3"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-04T01:14:52Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,1],"Message":"","SHA":"f9844f5ce4b3b8da36490d7f057f7c15b9d0ad24"},{"Author":"Auto","Date":"2026-01-03T01:03:34Z","File":["⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",89,